/-
The `360` packed keys of the two-qutrit dictionary, and their distinctness.

`QutritDict2.lean` packs each exponent table of `dict2` into one natural
number (`keyOf`, base `4`, one digit per digit string) and proves
`dict2Fast.map keyOf = keyLits` by evaluation. Distinctness of the tables
then reduces to `keyLits.Nodup`, which is `64,620` comparisons of literals.
That check lives here, in a module with no imports, because a module that
imports Mathlib starts at about `3.3 GB` of resident memory from the mapped
`.olean` files and the kernel's `Nodup` decision adds about `1.2 GB` more;
without the imports the same check peaks well under `2 GB`. The literals
were produced by `#eval (dict2Fast.map keyOf)` and the equality with the
computed keys is checked by the kernel in `QutritDict2.lean`, so nothing here
is trusted.
-/

